    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0287" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg181"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Japanese chargé d’ affaires.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-04-13">April 13,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Hioki</hi>: I inclose, in the form of a
                    memorandum, my response to the unsigned and undated memorandum you gave me
                    yesterday concerning the evacuation of Manchuria.</p>
                <pb facs="0288" n="182" xml:id="pg182"/>
                <p>While sending you this formal paper, I have the pleasure to acknowledge also your
                    personal and informal memorandum which accompanied the same and in which you
                    discuss the military and practical difficulties in the way of admitting
                    foreigners to the evacuated territory.</p>
                <p>I can not believe that American citizens will be likely to add to the
                    embarrassments of your military commanders in any appreciable degree.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for the information, I am, my dear Mr. Hioki,</p>
                <p>Faithfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d162-a1.xml" xpointer="d162-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
